Package: seny
Title: Sanity Checks for Differential Expression in Noisy Data
Version: 0.99.0
Authors@R:
    person("Samuel", "Morabito", email = "smorabit82@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-7768-4856"))
Description: For every cluster-by-contrast comparison in a multi-sample
    single-cell dataset, seny assesses whether a pseudobulk differential
    expression test is Adequate, Underpowered, Caution or Invalid, and explains
    why. The diagnostics are analytic: design validity and confounding
    (layer 1), pseudobulk quality (layer 2), variance structure and sensitivity
    (layer 4), with a minimum detectable effect per gene from a
    negative-binomial variance model, and subtype composition shifts that would
    make genes look differentially expressed on their own. No per-dataset simulation. The name is a
    backronym -- Sanity checks for differential gene Expression in NoisY data --
    and also the Catalan word for common sense.
